  "worked_solution": "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{\u2032},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x & \\,\u27f9\\,{u}^{\u2032}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{\u2032}=9\\sqrt{x} & \\,\u27f9\\,v=\\int 9\\sqrt{x}\\,dx=6{x}^{3/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}9\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}u{v}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}v{u}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x(6{x}^{3/2}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{6{x}^{3/2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({e}^{2})(6{({e}^{2})}^{3/2})-\\operatorname{ln}\u20611(6(1)^{3/2})]-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}6\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12{e}^{3}-4{x}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =12{e}^{3}-(4{({e}^{2})}^{3/2}-4(1)^{3/2}) \\\\  & =12{e}^{3}-4{e}^{3}+4 \\\\  & =8{e}^{3}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
